      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Idealistic hope\" sounds a bit dismissive of the market side though, don't u think? \n\nLook, if we're being real, if a country can just pollute more and pay workers pennies to get a competitive edge, the \"market\" isn't fixing anything, it's just rewarding bad behavior. It feels like the \"skepticism\" you're talking about is just a way for powerful nations to dodge responsibility for global standards by calling it \"protectionism.\" \n\nIf you were writing this briefing for the minister, would you actually recommend they vote for it, or is the \"economic friction\" too big of a deal? Like, is this treaty actually a viable solution or is it just a way for big players to control the rules of the game?",
